        ":question/id": "a91daa27-1897-5aea-9a99-012820a6dea2",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
        ":question/problem": "![](images/b3/b36ea011fb24a2bdad1002838450c888dfd4fabd06a5e4530e6ddf03ed7491c3.png)\n\nIn the diagram, $Z$ lies on the segment $GN$. The given vectors are $\\overrightarrow{OG}=h$ and $\\overrightarrow{ON}=d$. The lengths satisfy $GZ:ZN=4:5$.\n\nExpress $\\overrightarrow{ZO}$ in terms of $h$ and $d$. Fill in both coefficients, including their signs.\n\n$\\overrightarrow{ZO}=$ {{field-1}} $h+$ {{field-2}} $d$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First express both endpoint vectors in the directions away from $O$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{OG}=h\\qquad \\overrightarrow{ON}=d .\n$$\n\nTrace the path from $G$ through $O$ to $N$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{GN}=\\overrightarrow{GO}+\\overrightarrow{ON}=-h+d.\n$$\n\nThe ratio $GZ:ZN=4:5$ gives $9$ parts in the whole segment. Thus\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{GZ}=\\frac{4}{9}\\overrightarrow{GN}=\\frac{4}{9}(-h+d).\n$$\n\nAdd along the path $O\\to G\\to Z$ and collect coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overrightarrow{OZ}&=\\overrightarrow{OG}+\\overrightarrow{GZ}\\\\&=h+\\frac{4}{9}(-h+d)\\\\&=\\frac{5}{9}h+\\frac{4}{9}d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe requested vector has the reverse direction, so negate both coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{ZO}=-\\overrightarrow{OZ}=-\\frac{5}{9}h-\\frac{4}{9}d.\n$$",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "76d4a35d-8f3a-5fde-9014-f6f94077ba2f",
