        ":question/id": "fb3e8eda-0d7f-561e-ab3a-7a8d238c7f83",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
        ":question/problem": "![](images/41/4179a91e76bc5317e4c64a2a3c2c98b572faa7b299054146f06724144dadaa5c.png)\n\nIn the diagram, $P$ lies on the segment $HR$. The given vectors are $\\overrightarrow{OH}=r$ and $\\overrightarrow{RO}=a$. The lengths satisfy $HP:PR=1:1$.\n\nExpress $\\overrightarrow{PO}$ in terms of $r$ and $a$. Fill in both coefficients, including their signs.\n\n$\\overrightarrow{PO}=$ {{field-1}} $r+$ {{field-2}} $a$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First express both endpoint vectors in the directions away from $O$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{OH}=r\\qquad \\overrightarrow{OR}=-a .\n$$\n\nTrace the path from $H$ through $O$ to $R$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{HR}=\\overrightarrow{HO}+\\overrightarrow{OR}=-r-a.\n$$\n\nThe ratio $HP:PR=1:1$ gives $2$ parts in the whole segment. Thus\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{HP}=\\frac{1}{2}\\overrightarrow{HR}=\\frac{1}{2}(-r-a).\n$$\n\nAdd along the path $O\\to H\\to P$ and collect coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overrightarrow{OP}&=\\overrightarrow{OH}+\\overrightarrow{HP}\\\\&=r+\\frac{1}{2}(-r-a)\\\\&=\\frac{1}{2}r-\\frac{1}{2}a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe requested vector has the reverse direction, so negate both coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{PO}=-\\overrightarrow{OP}=-\\frac{1}{2}r+\\frac{1}{2}a.\n$$",
