        ":question/problem": "![](images/1c/1cc8caade45302ca676960270b0cd06b5eb7bad7f7a4ce7df84e0e2e57eba276.png)\n\nIn the diagram, $Z$ lies on the segment $BP$. The given vectors are $\\overrightarrow{BO}=k$ and $\\overrightarrow{OP}=f$. The lengths satisfy $BZ:ZP=1:3$.\n\nExpress $\\overrightarrow{OZ}$ in terms of $k$ and $f$. Fill in both coefficients, including their signs.\n\n$\\overrightarrow{OZ}=$ {{field-1}} $k+$ {{field-2}} $f$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First express both endpoint vectors in the directions away from $O$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{OB}=-k\\qquad \\overrightarrow{OP}=f .\n$$\n\nTrace the path from $B$ through $O$ to $P$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{BP}=\\overrightarrow{BO}+\\overrightarrow{OP}=k+f.\n$$\n\nThe ratio $BZ:ZP=1:3$ gives $4$ parts in the whole segment. Thus\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{BZ}=\\frac{1}{4}\\overrightarrow{BP}=\\frac{1}{4}(k+f).\n$$\n\nAdd along the path $O\\to B\\to Z$ and collect coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overrightarrow{OZ}&=\\overrightarrow{OB}+\\overrightarrow{BZ}\\\\&=-k+\\frac{1}{4}(k+f)\\\\&=-\\frac{3}{4}k+\\frac{1}{4}f.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
