        ":question/problem": "![](images/2b/2bc7f8a30eb99f7538ac0e56de515c8fabfee7315c0816934f7a69559d8d8fc4.png)\n\nIn the diagram, $P$ lies on the segment $LV$. The given vectors are $\\overrightarrow{LO}=k$ and $\\overrightarrow{OV}=h$. The lengths satisfy $LP:PV=4:3$.\n\nExpress $\\overrightarrow{PO}$ in terms of $k$ and $h$. Fill in both coefficients, including their signs.\n\n$\\overrightarrow{PO}=$ {{field-1}} $k+$ {{field-2}} $h$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First express both endpoint vectors in the directions away from $O$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{OL}=-k\\qquad \\overrightarrow{OV}=h .\n$$\n\nTrace the path from $L$ through $O$ to $V$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{LV}=\\overrightarrow{LO}+\\overrightarrow{OV}=k+h.\n$$\n\nThe ratio $LP:PV=4:3$ gives $7$ parts in the whole segment. Thus\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{LP}=\\frac{4}{7}\\overrightarrow{LV}=\\frac{4}{7}(k+h).\n$$\n\nAdd along the path $O\\to L\\to P$ and collect coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overrightarrow{OP}&=\\overrightarrow{OL}+\\overrightarrow{LP}\\\\&=-k+\\frac{4}{7}(k+h)\\\\&=-\\frac{3}{7}k+\\frac{4}{7}h.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe requested vector has the reverse direction, so negate both coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{PO}=-\\overrightarrow{OP}=\\frac{3}{7}k-\\frac{4}{7}h.\n$$",
